Myth: Long before the first dawn, Kael, a deaf mortal artisan, forged radiant bells from pure silver and gold. When the earth trembled, their deep vibrations coaxed rivers of shimmering light from the barren, early world, warming the frozen valleys. Terra, the gentle spirit of the deep soil, cherished these luminous tremors. But the Dark Serpent, a bitter entity ruling the subterranean chasms in eternal gloom, despised the comforting glow. Rising in a suffocating shroud of darkness, the Serpent snatched his bells and shattered them within the jagged, lightless trenches of the ancient Abyss.

Plunged into absolute cold, the heartbroken, lonely artisan wept in the dark, silent valleys. Refusing to let the warmth die, Terra scoured the freezing depths, gathering up every glowing, shattered shard. She guided Kael down into the winding underground caverns. With his scarred hands, Kael spent years reshaping the dormant tunnels into a massive, interconnected labyrinth, embedding the starry fragments deep within the stone walls.

When the forging was finally finished, Terra summoned the deep geothermal pulses of the world. A roaring, magnificent symphony of light and tremor erupted. The mighty resonance banished the gloom forever, transforming the underworld into an immense sanctuary of humming, eternal starlight.
